00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:16.250
This is a user
interface we actually

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.800
released just about
a few months back,

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:21.620
and it is centered
around the API lifecycle.

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:23.400
So in this case,
I'll do a little bit

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.850
of level setting here.

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:27.420
I'm connected to
the demo file ORG.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:30.050
Think about ORG as a
short for an organization.

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:33.770
And it's the container where I
as a business unit, or a team,

00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:37.970
or a company if it is small
enough, will build all my APIs

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:40.107
and add some policies.

00:14:40.107 --> 00:14:41.690
The very first thing
we're going to do

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:45.370
is start off with taking a spec.

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:47.900
In this case, I'm going
to take the liberty

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:53.830
of leveraging a spec that is
called Open API for hotels.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:58.050
It's a very simple spec
which is sitting somewhere

00:14:58.050 --> 00:14:59.660
in the internet.

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:02.210
In this case, it happens
to be just a simple gist

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.020
on our GitHub account.

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:06.020
So let's go to the
Apigee Edge screen.

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:08.750
GREG BRAIL: So that spec, that
